<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 13:49:17 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Nepal: Thousands still missing as death toll rises</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-death-toll-rises</link><description>
Nepalese authorities announced on Sunday that the provisional death toll from the devastating floods had risen to more than 730, with nearly 2,500 people still missing.

Among the thousands of people missing is the husband of a 22-year-old woman, who is still waiting for him to return. Like tens of thousands of Nepalese people in recent days, she went to one of the country’s medical centres to find out whether her husband was among those whose bodies had been recovered in recent days. Caitlin Brown reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac96234e-a454-11f1-b965-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-110309-110452-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac96234e-a454-11f1-b965-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-110309-110452-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2739594-a454-11f1-baaa-49bcf89cf529</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 10:04:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal: Glacial collapse leaves 3,000 missing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-glacial-collapse-leaves-3-000-missing</link><description>
Rescue and relief efforts in Nepal and Tibet have been hampered this Sunday by heavy rain and rising river levels. The latest figures following Wednesday’s flash floods put the death toll at 750, while more than 3,000 people remain missing. Nepal’s disaster authorities are urging rescue teams to “exercise caution”, warning that bad weather, swollen rivers and the threat of further flooding could hamper operations. Shazab Wahlah reports from the town of Bidur.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4cbf6d4-a452-11f1-9422-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-100419-100544-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4cbf6d4-a452-11f1-9422-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-100419-100544-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">caebbc84-a452-11f1-b9bf-49bcf89cf529</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:16:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Death toll rises as 3,000 remain missing in Nepal, China</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/death-toll-rises-as-3-000-remain-missing-in-nepal-china</link><description>
Rescue and relief efforts in Nepal and Tibet have been hampered this Sunday by heavy rain and rising river levels. The latest figures following Wednesday’s flash floods put the death toll at 750, while more than 3,000 people remain missing. Nepal’s disaster authorities are urging rescue teams to “exercise caution”, warning that bad weather, swollen rivers and the threat of further flooding could hamper operations. Shazab Wahlah reports from the town of Bidur.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ca458a7e-a44a-11f1-927b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-090302-090512-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ca458a7e-a44a-11f1-927b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-090302-090512-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf7d2614-a44a-11f1-bae8-ef30ccbee3a0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 08:37:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Putin, Xi set for Central Asia summit as Russia and China seek to counter Western influence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-putin-xi-set-for-central-asia-summit-as-russia-china-seek-to-counter-western-influence</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir Putin and Chinese President Xi Jinping are due in Kyrgyzstan on Monday for a two-day summit, joined by the leaders of Iran and India. The gathering comes as the group seeks to project a united front amid wars in Ukraine and Iran and growing tensions with the West.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32f6bdfa-a436-11f1-a03d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26140554039627.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32f6bdfa-a436-11f1-a03d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26140554039627.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bda6ad80-a435-11f1-9783-ed09ccae7966</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 05:51:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32f6bdfa-a436-11f1-a03d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26140554039627.jpg">© Alexander Kazakov/Pool Sputnik K</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Nepal-Tibet floods live: Nepal begins mass burials as flood death toll surpasses 780</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-nepal-tibet-floods-live-at-least-750-dead-as-death-toll-rises</link><description>
Nepal on Sunday began temporarily burying some of the hundreds of bodies recovered from devastating floods after taking DNA samples and marking the remains so families can identify and retrieve them later. Rescue efforts entered a fifth day, with heavy overnight rain and rising rivers hampering attempts to reach hydropower workers believed to be trapped in tunnels. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0035e18e-a463-11f1-9afb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6UC2WP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0035e18e-a463-11f1-9afb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6UC2WP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">997c7d82-a42f-11f1-a21d-673daa4be3df</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 04:59:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0035e18e-a463-11f1-9afb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6UC2WP.jpg">© Prakash Mathema, AFP</source><dc:creator>Natasha LI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Missing toll from Nepal, China flood nears 3,000 as race for survivors continues</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260829-missing-toll-from-nepal-china-flood-nears-3-000-as-race-for-survivors-continues</link><description>
Rescuers in Nepal and China on Saturday continued to search for the nearly 3,000 people missing after devastating flooding along the border with China engulfed entire villages earlier this week. At least 682 bodies were recovered in both countries, including 675 in Nepal and seven in China.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e22b113e-a3e3-11f1-b707-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6TD3PQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e22b113e-a3e3-11f1-b707-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6TD3PQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">191f0222-a3e4-11f1-8edd-1db0309f0cfc</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 20:12:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e22b113e-a3e3-11f1-b707-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6TD3PQ.jpg">© Manan Vatsyayana, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘Extremely risky operations’: Rescuers work amid threat of river banks bursting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/extremely-risky-operations-rescuers-work-amid-threat-of-river-banks-bursting</link><description>
Nearly 3,000 people remained missing on Saturday, while 682 deaths had been confirmed after flash floods and landslides hit the Nepal-Tibet border. Rescue operations remain risky as a lake formed upstream by the floods threatens to burst its banks. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/015888a2-a3bc-11f1-82bf-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-170217-170456-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/015888a2-a3bc-11f1-82bf-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-170217-170456-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">06dad5f0-a3bc-11f1-9539-775873edb3f6</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:22:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Rescue operations ongoing as death toll continues to rise</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/rescue-operations-ongoing-as-death-toll-continues-to-rise</link><description>
Most arrive with nothing except the clothes they are wearing. As rescue efforts in communities buried by catastrophic flash floods along the border between Nepal and China entered their fourth day Saturday, authorities continued finding survivors and transporting them to safety. At relief centers, as some arrive, families wait anxiously for news of their loved ones as the death toll and the number of people unaccounted for continued to rise.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d702860-a3a5-11f1-80c0-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-140548-140738-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d702860-a3a5-11f1-80c0-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-140548-140738-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a6036974-a3a5-11f1-b092-f30ef7d965b0</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:37:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepali army uses helicopters to rescue flood survivors</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepali-army-uses-helicopters-to-rescue-flood-survivors</link><description>
With roads damaged by the deadly floods, the Nepali army is using helicopters to carry out rescue operations and transport survivors to safety. Meanwhile, skies remain overcast, with more rain expected in the coming hours, raising concerns about further flooding. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73840a0a-a394-11f1-8059-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-120715-120817-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73840a0a-a394-11f1-8059-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-120715-120817-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">78b70284-a394-11f1-a505-d1c2be3b23b1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:32:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal army races to rescue more than 100 trapped in hydropower tunnel after floods</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-army-races-to-rescue-more-than-100-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnel-after-floods</link><description>
Nepali army rescue teams were using drilling equipment on Saturday seeking to rescue more than 100 people trapped inside a hydropower tunnel, three days after devastating floods struck the site.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b381f60-a383-11f1-b57d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-100137-100259-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b381f60-a383-11f1-b57d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-100137-100259-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1041ee82-a383-11f1-984d-a176131393b9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 08:50:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>UN, Nepal warn of climate threat after flood death toll tops 680</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260829-nepal-tibet-floods-live-death-toll-passes-600-nearly-2-500-people-still-missing</link><description>
Nepal's foreign minister and the UN climate chief on Saturday warned of the growing threat from climate change to the Himalayas, three days after devastating floods swept along the border with China, engulfing entire villages. At least 675 people were killed in Nepal, according to the country's disaster authority. Another seven people were confirmed dead in Tibet, Chinese state media reported. Read our blog to see how all the day's events unfolded. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/622b729c-a3e0-11f1-9572-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26241508993409.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/622b729c-a3e0-11f1-9572-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26241508993409.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5df0d2e0-a367-11f1-8136-513a32e153e1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 05:06:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/622b729c-a3e0-11f1-9572-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26241508993409.jpg">AP Photo/Rajesh Kumar Singh - Rajesh Kumar Singh</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal: Families cling to hope as nearly 1,000 remain missing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-families-cling-to-hope-as-nearly-1-000-remain-missing</link><description>
Nepal's confirmed death toll has risen to at least 538, but families are still searching hospitals and disaster zones in the hope their loved ones will be found alive, with nearly 1,000 people still missing. More than 3,700 people have been rescued so far, though destroyed roads, bridges and thick mud continue to hamper search efforts.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d92d8b2e-a2fe-11f1-8dce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260828-170152-170321-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d92d8b2e-a2fe-11f1-8dce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260828-170152-170321-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ddf29c80-a2fe-11f1-97e4-fb49be6c8bf6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:56:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal: Relief camp shelters grieving families</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-relief-camp-shelters-grieving-families</link><description>
Around 500 people are sheltering at a monastery-turned-relief camp in northern Kathmandu, where many families are still in shock after losing their homes and loved ones in the devastating Nepal floods. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah reports from the camp as rescue teams continue searching for nearly 1,000 missing people, with operations set to continue through the night.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f19d2d20-a1e8-11f1-90f9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T054155Z-1329930245-RC2T6NALUMIO-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f19d2d20-a1e8-11f1-90f9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T054155Z-1329930245-RC2T6NALUMIO-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5410a830-a2eb-11f1-8039-4ba3ad3be82c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:20:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Rescuers grapple with a mountain of challenges after the Nepal-Tibet floods</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-rescuers-grapple-with-mountain-of-challenges-after-the-nepal-tibet-floods</link><description>
Emergency services are rushing to find survivors and treat the wounded after a devastating flash flood on the border of Nepal and Tibet on Wednesday killed more than 500 people, with over a thousand still missing. But the remote and rugged terrain, as well as the risk of further flooding from upstream lakes formed by piles of debris, make their work as delicate as it is dangerous.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66f1c974-a21a-11f1-b5fb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/rescue-nepal.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66f1c974-a21a-11f1-b5fb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/rescue-nepal.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89715fd6-a2e3-11f1-9545-bfe6b30a202f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:14:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66f1c974-a21a-11f1-b5fb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/rescue-nepal.jpg">© Arun Sankar, AFP</source><dc:creator>Sébastian SEIBT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal floods explained: The chain of events behind the disaster</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-explained-the-chain-of-events-behind-the-disaster</link><description>
A glacier broke apart. An ice and rock avalanche followed. Then came an earthquake, before a landslide triggered devastating floods that tore through kilometres of valley. This is what happened along the Nepal-China border, where rescue teams are still trying to recover survivors 48 hours after the catastrophe. FRANCE 24 breaks down the chain of events and the scientific explanations behind the disaster.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30b8c788-a15a-11f1-b017-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26238334534782.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30b8c788-a15a-11f1-b017-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26238334534782.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3954b24e-a2db-11f1-b961-bf53a2232917</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:48:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Revisited</category><title>Japan's controversial WWII heroes: How one kamikaze pilot escaped certain death</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260828-japan-s-controversial-wwii-heroes-how-one-kamikaze-pilot-escaped-certain-death</link><description>
Towards the end of World War II, as US troops advanced across the Pacific, Japan resorted to a desperate strategy: kamikaze attacks. Thousands of Japanese pilots, with an average age of just 21, were ordered to crash their explosive-laden planes into enemy ships. More than 3,800 pilots gave up their lives, killing over 7,000 allied naval personnel. Our reporter Mélodie Sforza met one of the last surviving former kamikaze pilots.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c9603dfa-a1f9-11f1-9bd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-280826-EN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c9603dfa-a1f9-11f1-9bd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-280826-EN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce7d3bd0-a091-11f1-ae26-5574425f8dd8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:42:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Alexis BREGERE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal flood survivors rescued from hydropower tunnel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-flood-survivors-rescued-from-hydropower-tunnel</link><description>
Nepali soldiers rescued around 100 people trapped inside a flooded hydropower tunnel as the death toll from the Nepal-China floods continued to climb, with more than 1,500 people still missing. Rescue efforts were briefly suspended over fears that an overflowing landslide lake could trigger more flooding, while families across the disaster zone continue searching for loved ones.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/91d2d728-a2d8-11f1-a6cb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260828-130127-130247-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/91d2d728-a2d8-11f1-a6cb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260828-130127-130247-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">974127d2-a2d8-11f1-8aa6-bf53a2232917</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:38:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>'Ran for our lives': Flood survivors recount terrifying escape from Nepal-Tibet disaster</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-ran-for-our-lives-flood-survivors-recount-terrifying-escape-from-nepal-tibet-disaster</link><description>
Survivors of the catastrophic flash floods in Nepal and Tibet, some still missing friends and family members, shared harrowing accounts of their escape from raging floodwaters that brought devastation to the Himalayan border region, leaving more than 550 people dead and some 1,500 missing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4877f86-a2a4-11f1-8c93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/a445c491a2511f5d6e49b86a241ebbb831600f74.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4877f86-a2a4-11f1-8c93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/a445c491a2511f5d6e49b86a241ebbb831600f74.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">559378e0-a2d7-11f1-a454-f321a3274e19</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 11:55:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4877f86-a2a4-11f1-8c93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/a445c491a2511f5d6e49b86a241ebbb831600f74.jpg">© Arun Sankar, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal and Tibet : around 93,000 people affected, according to the Red Cross</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-and-tibet-around-93-000-people-affected-according-to-the-red-cross</link><description>
The death toll continues to rise in the Nepal and Tibet floods as the situation remains fast-moving. The Red Cross says around 93,000 people have been affected. International aid is arriving from several countries, but rescue efforts have been hampered by the difficulty of coordinating operations in the remote Himalayan terrain. The epicentre of the disaster was only reached 48 hours after the floods began. FRANCE 24's Jamie Smith-Maillet has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c32e947a-a241-11f1-8ef7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/eeb7d109036331a0c0d020367f59af082ea071b3w.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c32e947a-a241-11f1-8ef7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/eeb7d109036331a0c0d020367f59af082ea071b3w.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0ae01850-a2cb-11f1-b51e-131f88726134</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 11:42:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal: Army rescues hundreds trapped in tunnel as flood risk reignites</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260828-nepal-army-rescues-hundreds-trapped-in-tunnel-as-flood-risk-reignites</link><description>
#Rescue operations are underway in #Nepal after devastating #floods killed hundreds and left more than 1,400 missing. The #RedCross has also raised concern over humanitarian #aid, as it estimates nearly 100,000 people were affected by the #disaster.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9071bc6c-a2cb-11f1-8eff-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NEpal-rescue-updates.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9071bc6c-a2cb-11f1-8eff-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NEpal-rescue-updates.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aca929b0-a2cb-11f1-8b3c-131f88726134</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 10:36:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal flash floods: 'Very challenging' for survivors who have lost their homes and their families</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260828-nepal-flash-floods-very-challenging-for-survivors-who-have-lost-their-homes-and-their-families</link><description>
Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Sunita Sharma, Head of Programs of Karuna-Shechen. While Nepal has considerable experience responding to natural disasters, the scale of the present devastation exposes a deeper challenge: Placing greater emphasis on preparedness. The immediate priorities are clear: finding those still missing and providing survivors with drinking water, food, shelter, clothing and medicine. But recovery cannot end there. Ultimately, they will need to rebuild confidence and entire communities. Given the scale of the destruction, that process could take years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/528dfd0a-a2c3-11f1-81b1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260828-091712-092608-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/528dfd0a-a2c3-11f1-81b1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260828-091712-092608-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">57f16642-a2c3-11f1-9011-09eed1c79a0a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:50:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal flood disaster reconstructed minute by minute</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-flood-disaster-reconstructed-minute-by-minute</link><description>
New satellite imagery and video analysis show the deadly Nepal floods began when part of a glacier near the Chinese border collapsed, triggering a debris flow that raced downstream at up to 150 km/h and devastated communities over more than 80 kilometres. Scientists are still piecing together the exact sequence of events, while authorities warn the disaster may not be over as a newly formed lake upstream has started to overflow.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6cd2bda-a2bd-11f1-9da3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260828-090346-090618-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6cd2bda-a2bd-11f1-9da3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260828-090346-090618-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fcadfcf0-a2bd-11f1-9205-97a22bddeee2</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:22:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Reporters</category><title>China's lost children: Adoptees search for answers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260828-china-s-lost-children-adoptees-search-for-answers</link><description>
At the height of China's controversial one-child policy, children were torn away from their birth families and put up for adoption. FRANCE 24's Yena Lee follows one adoptee, now an adult, who is on a quest to find out more about her background.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ada7234-a146-11f1-bf9e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Reporters-ChineAdoption-FR-EN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ada7234-a146-11f1-bf9e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Reporters-ChineAdoption-FR-EN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd5195ac-a05d-11f1-96c2-9153919de290</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:19:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yena LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>In Tibet and Nepal, 'the most pressing fear is that the death toll could rise'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/in-tibet-and-nepal-the-most-pressing-fear-is-that-the-death-toll-could-rise</link><description>
At least 472 people have been killed and more than 1,500 remain missing after devastating flash floods hit the Himalayan border between Nepal and China, where over 3,250 people have already been evacuated by helicopter. As rescuers race to find survivors, one of the biggest fears is that the death toll will continue to rise, with authorities also warning that an overflowing lake upstream could trigger more flooding. FRANCE 24's Navodita Kumari has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02f59162-a242-11f1-a302-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T120902Z-886945342-RC207NAPVBUI-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02f59162-a242-11f1-a302-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T120902Z-886945342-RC207NAPVBUI-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed68d3dc-a2b8-11f1-9307-3536965512b5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:16:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Countries step up aid for Nepal flood disaster</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/countries-step-up-aid-for-nepal-flood-disaster</link><description>
Countries including South Korea, India, China, the UK and the EU are ramping up rescue efforts and humanitarian aid after the devastating Nepal-China floods, with hundreds of foreign nationals still missing. Relief operations remain difficult in the Himalayan terrain, while authorities warn that a lake formed by the disaster could burst and trigger a second wave of flooding.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e40d538-a2bc-11f1-b7fd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260828-100305-100443-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e40d538-a2bc-11f1-b7fd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260828-100305-100443-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">73044816-a2bc-11f1-a445-97a22bddeee2</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:00:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Rescuers search for hundreds still missing in Nepal-Tibet disaster area as death toll climbs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-nepal-tibet-live-china-warns-lake-formed-by-mudslide-on-nepal-border-could-breach</link><description>
Rescuers in Tibet reached the main area wiped out by a devastating mudslide this week, Chinese state media reported, as the search for missing people battled treacherous conditions. The devastating flooding in Nepal and Tibet has claimed more than 580 lives and left more than 2,400 missing. Read our live blog to see how all the day's events unfolded. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/687d1484-a2ff-11f1-99ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26240453035252.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/687d1484-a2ff-11f1-99ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26240453035252.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8c136530-a262-11f1-afa7-0379bbe3c380</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 03:03:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/687d1484-a2ff-11f1-99ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26240453035252.jpg">© Dar Yasin, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Number of people missing in deadly Nepal, Tibet floods jumps past 2,400</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260828-number-of-people-missing-in-deadly-nepal-tibet-floods-jumps-past-2-400</link><description>
Nepal’s disaster authority sharply raised the number of missing to 1,924 on Friday, including 517 foreigners, two days after devastating floods that killed at least 586 in the country. A further 558 people are also reported missing in Tibet, where Chinese officials say at least five people have died.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4e21d02-a2c4-11f1-a916-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/bf142d70758c87ebc7d23df62d05579504d55f35.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4e21d02-a2c4-11f1-a916-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/bf142d70758c87ebc7d23df62d05579504d55f35.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">81f110ac-a28a-11f1-806c-fbc8f44ff03d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 02:45:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4e21d02-a2c4-11f1-a916-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/bf142d70758c87ebc7d23df62d05579504d55f35.jpg">© CNS via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title><![CDATA[Red Cross mobilises in Nepal following natural disaster: 'Entire villages & communities washed out']]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/red-cross-mobilises-in-nepal-following-natural-disaster-entire-villages-communities-washed-out</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Tommaso Della Longa, Spokesperson for the International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies. The immediate challenge in Nepal is not only the scale of destruction, explains Della Longa, but the difficulty of reaching communities whose roads, bridges and communications have been swept away. Their priority remains search and rescue and the delivery of life-saving assistance, even as they begin preparing for longer-term recovery. Yet this is also a deeply human crisis for first responders: local Red Cross volunteers are supporting their own communities while some have themselves lost homes or relatives.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ff22d14-a23e-11f1-ab89-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260827-170055-170928-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ff22d14-a23e-11f1-ab89-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260827-170055-170928-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84ff95d0-a23e-11f1-af1d-e1aef03a70db</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:53:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Pakistan: Protests continue in Azad Kashmir despite repression and internet blackout</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260827-pakistan-protests-continue-in-azad-kashmir-despite-repression-and-internet-blackout</link><description>
Harshly repressed protests that have shaken Pakistan-administered Kashmir since early June have continued through local legislative elections held in July and August. With internet access cut off and access by foreign media restricted, local residents are attempting to report on the situation on the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/870e0b6c-a131-11f1-927a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-Article-KAshmir.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/870e0b6c-a131-11f1-927a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-Article-KAshmir.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0817d42e-a09f-11f1-8620-9d82936aa880</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:04:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/870e0b6c-a131-11f1-927a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-Article-KAshmir.jpg">© Facebook/Hamza Naseer</source><dc:creator>Marguerite MARAMICI</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Why were so many Indian pilgrims in Tibet during the Himalayan mudslide disaster?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/why-were-so-many-indian-pilgrims-in-tibet-during-the-himalayan-mudslide-disaster</link><description>
Hundreds of Indian nationals are missing in Nepal and Tibet following a catastrophic Himalayan flood. They include several pilgrims doing the Kailash Mansarovar Yatra pilgrimage to Mount Kailash, a mountain in Tibet that holds sacred significance for Hinduism, Buddhism, Jainism and the Tibetan Bon religion, explains FRANCE 24’s Leela Jacinto.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c813854-a21d-11f1-aab6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260827-150538-150926-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c813854-a21d-11f1-aab6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260827-150538-150926-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21b2f75e-a21d-11f1-b7bf-23b04c942e15</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 13:57:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
